# =============================================================================
# Daylio API Server — Docker build context exclusions (FASE 0 / Task 0.6,
# verified in FASE 7 / Task 7.5).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Goal: the build context must contain ONLY what the multi-stage Dockerfile
# actually copies, so the image stays lean and no local artifact, secret or
# test fixture can ever leak into it.
#
# What the Dockerfile needs from the context (never exclude these):
#   requirements.lock          -> stage "build"  (pip install -r)
#   src/                       -> stage "runtime" (the application package)
#   version.ini                -> stage "runtime" (version metadata)
#   config/config.example.yml  -> stage "runtime" (default config schema)
#
# Everything else is excluded: VCS metadata, virtualenvs, caches, byte-code,
# the SQLite runtime data, tests, sample data, docs, CI and local secrets.
# =============================================================================

# --- VCS / CI ----------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitea/
.github/
.gitattributes

# --- virtualenvs & build artifacts -------------------------------------------
.venv
venv
env
build
dist
*.egg-info
src/*.egg-info

# --- python byte-code & tool caches -----------------------------------------
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.so
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- runtime data (SQLite source of truth) & local secrets -------------------
data/
data.db
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
config/config.yml
config/users.yml

# --- test / sample / documentation / tooling --------------------------------
tests/
sample-data/
docs/
scripts/
*.md
!README.md

# --- docker & dev files (the Dockerfile itself is in the context by design) --
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
requirements.in
requirements.txt
requirements-dev.in
Makefile
.idea/
.vscode/
